# Unraid template conventions

Full guidance with sources: `@docs/UNRAID-TEMPLATE-GUIDE.md`. The short version:

- `<Container version="2">`. Every path, variable, and port is a one-line `<Config>`. No legacy `<Networking>`, `<Data>`, or `<Environment>` blocks.
- `Type="Path"` maps a host folder; `Type="Variable"` sets an environment variable; `Type="Port"` only under bridge networking. `Mask="true"` on secrets, with an empty default.
- Host networking means no `Type="Port"` entries, so the README and the port field's description must spell out the TCP/UDP forwards and that the port must be free on the Unraid host.
- `<Overview>` is what users see; keep `<Description>`, field descriptions, and `README.md` consistent with it. Escape `&` as `&amp;`.
- `<TemplateURL>`, `<Icon>`, `<Support>`, `<Project>`, and the `ca_profile.xml` URLs point at this repository's `main` branch.
- A wrapper entrypoint validates form values, writes files atomically with restrictive modes, then execs the upstream entrypoint with arguments unchanged.
- A parsed XML file is only well-formed. Say so; Unraid behavior needs an install test.
